r=add(16,'Creamed Young Carrots with Yolk and Parsley',4,55,'Young carrots cook gently in very little liquid, then receive a small rich cream-and-yolk coating.',[dict(carrot(500),name='young carrots, scrubbed and trimmed'),water(1000,'blanchwater'),butter(14),water(30),salt(2),pepper(),cream(60),parsley(2),yolks(2)],['Bring {{blanchwater}} to a boil. Add {{carrot}}, blanch for 5 minutes, drain and cool just enough to handle. Rub or scrape away the skins, then cut into thin rounds.','Put {{butter}}, {{water}}, {{salt}} and {{pepper}} in a saucepan. Add the carrots, cover and cook very gently for 20–30 minutes until tender; add a small splash of water if needed to prevent scorching.','Heat {{cream}} and {{parsley}} in a small pan until steaming. Whisk {{yolks}} in a bowl and gradually whisk in the hot cream.','Pour the egg-cream mixture over the carrots and stir gently over low heat until the sauce reaches 71°C (160°F), without boiling. Serve immediately.'],'Missing carrot and blanching-water quantities are supplied. The source small cream-to-yolk ratio is retained, with controlled heating instead of an unspecified scant minute.')
r=add(17,'Twice-Cooked Carrots in Light Stock Sauce',4,65,'Whole carrots are boiled, diced and simmered again in light stock before a small milk-and-butter finish.',[carrot(500),water(1200),salt(3),dict(stock(400),name='light unsalted prepared beef stock'),milk(30),butter(14),flour(8),pepper()],['Put {{carrot}} whole in a saucepan with {{water}} and {{salt}}. Bring to a simmer and cook for 20–30 minutes until nearly tender. Drain and cool just enough to handle.','Cut the carrots into 1 cm cubes. Put in a saucepan with {{stock}} and simmer for 10–20 minutes until completely tender.','Mash {{butter}} with {{flour}}. Stir {{milk}} and {{pepper}} into the carrots, add the butter-flour paste in small pieces and simmer for 5–7 minutes, stirring, until lightly thickened.'],'The two-stage whole-then-diced method is retained. Modern times allow checking tenderness earlier than the source 45-minute first boil. Missing carrot and stock amounts are supplied.')
r=add(18,'Mrkev se Zeleným Hráškem (Carrots with Green Peas)',6,45,'Dill and sour cream flavor tender carrots arranged around separately cooked parsley peas.',[carrot(500),I('peas',600,'g','shelled green peas, fresh or frozen','Use the same weight of thawed frozen peas; cook just until tender.'),butter(40),sugar(8),salt(4),flour(16),stock(400),I('sourcream',60,'g','sour cream','Use the same weight of a plant-based sour cream suited to cooking.'),I('dill',5,'g','fresh dill, finely chopped','Use 2 g dried dill, or omit.'),parsley(5)],['Cut {{carrot}} into thin 5 cm sticks. Melt {{butter|0.5}} in a saucepan, add the carrots, {{sugar|0.5}}, {{salt|0.5}} and {{stock|0.5}}. Cover and simmer for 15–20 minutes until nearly tender.','Mix {{flour|0.5}} with {{sourcream}} until smooth, stir into the carrots and simmer gently for 5 minutes. Stir in {{dill}}.','In a second saucepan, melt {{butter|0.5}}, stir in {{flour|0.5}} and cook for 2 minutes. Gradually stir in {{stock|0.5}}, {{sugar|0.5}} and {{salt|0.5}}. Add {{peas}} and simmer for 5–10 minutes until tender; stir in {{parsley}}.','Arrange the parsley peas in the center of a warm dish and spoon the dill carrots around them in a wreath.'],'The source quart of peas becomes a disclosed 600 g shelled weight. Missing amounts are supplied. Two separate pans and the contrasting herb/cream finishes are retained; the pea roux is cooked before adding peas to avoid flour lumps.')
r=add(21,'Ensalada de Zanahoria with Blanched Onion',4,75,'Cold carrot slices and briefly blanched onion are dressed with parsley, pepper and a simple vinaigrette.',[carrot(500),water(1000),salt(3),onion(80),water(500,'onionwater'),parsley(5),pepper(),I('oliveoil',25,'ml','olive oil','Use the same volume of neutral vegetable oil.'),I('vinegar',15,'ml','white wine vinegar','Use the same volume of cider vinegar.')],[boil('5 mm rounds','10–15'),'Spread the carrots in a shallow container and refrigerate promptly until cold, about 30 minutes.','Thinly slice {{onion}}. Bring {{onionwater}} to a boil, add the onion for 1 minute, then drain, rinse briefly under cold drinking water and squeeze gently dry.','Whisk {{oliveoil}}, {{vinegar}}, {{pepper}} and {{parsley}} together. Toss with the cold carrots and onion. Refrigerate until serving.'],'The same-book beet salad was recovered: cook/cool/slice vegetables and blanch/rinse onion. That preparation is now explicit. The unspecified dressing is supplied as a modern vinaigrette; its formula was not present in the source.','Salads')
