r=add(22,'Zanahorias Salteadas in Lard',4,30,'Thin young carrot slices sauté in a modest amount of lard until tender and lightly golden.',[carrot(500),lard(25),salt(2)],['Cut {{carrot}} into even 3 mm rounds. Heat {{lard}} in a wide skillet over medium-low heat.','Add the carrots in a shallow layer with {{salt}}. Cook for 15–20 minutes, tossing often, until tender and lightly golden. Work in batches if needed; lower the heat if they brown before softening.','If the pan dries while the carrots remain firm, add a small splash of water and cover for 2–3 minutes, then uncover to evaporate the moisture. Serve hot.'],'The missing preparation is made explicit as thin slicing. Carrot, lard and salt amounts are supplied. A short covered water finish is a modern fallback for firmer carrots, not a recovered source step.')
r=add(23,'Zanahorias Tempranas a la Crema',4,40,'Thin young carrot rounds braise with herbs and finish in cream thickened with egg yolks.',[carrot(500),water(60),butter(20),salt(2),pepper(),parsley(5),cream(120),yolks(2),milk(15)],['Slice {{carrot}} into 3 mm rounds. Put in a saucepan with {{water}}, {{butter}}, {{salt}}, {{pepper}} and {{parsley}}. Cover and simmer gently for 15–20 minutes until nearly tender, adding a small splash of water if needed.','Add {{cream}} and cook gently for 5 minutes until the carrots are tender.','Whisk {{yolks}} with {{milk}}. Slowly whisk in a little hot sauce, return to the pan and stir gently over low heat until the sauce reaches 71°C (160°F), without boiling. Serve hot.'],'A half-cup of cream becomes 120 ml, and parsley represents the unspecified fine herbs. Missing amounts and controlled egg cooking are supplied. The source double-volume milk alternative is retained.')
